TI  - Process Mining Techniques Utilizing ChatGPT: A Comparative Analysis with Disco Software on Call Center Log Data
PY  - 2024
T2  - International Conference on ICT and Knowledge Engineering
DO  - 10.1109/ICTKE62841.2024.10787195
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85215094144&doi=10.1109%2fICTKE62841.2024.10787195&partnerID=40&md5=dc4686c2e0396b3e37e064785ed3a222
AB  - This paper presents a novel methodology for applying process mining techniques to an unstructured call log dataset, CallcenterExample. csv. The dataset, which has been simplified and anonymized to preserve confidentiality, serves as a representative sample of actual call center records. The study employs the Code Interpreter in conjunction with the PM4PY process mining library running on ChatGPT, as well as the Fluxicon Disco software, to conduct a comprehensive process analysis. The analysis highlights the capabilities of the PM4PY library within the Code Interpreter framework, demonstrating its effectiveness in process analysis and visualization. In addition, a comparative evaluation is performed using Disco software to assess the respective strengths and limitations of both tools. The results indicate that while Disco offers distinct advantages, such as its intuitive interface and ease of use, facilitating in-depth process visualization and co-analysis, the ChatGPT-based approach delivers more granular insights, particularly through detailed analysis and actionable recommendations related to call center operations. The study underscores the complementary nature of these tools, with Disco excelling in facilitating user-driven exploration and visualization, while the ChatGPT-PM4PY integration offers advanced analytical depth. By employing process mining techniques, this research contributes valuable insights into the operational dynamics of call centers, demonstrating the potential for integrating these tools in enhancing process efficiency and decision-making. © 2024 IEEE.
