UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85184851623&doi=10.1109%2fICTKE58576.2023.10401333&partnerID=40&md5=c298f81bc56ed72ab4d59e9270aafd6a
AB  - This research presents a comprehensive analysis of sales systems in quotation preparation, focusing on identifying underlying issues contributing to delays and deviations from predefined targets. This investigation is facilitated by applying process mining techniques, which enable the discovery and visualization of actual bottlenecks within an IT equipment sales company's sales system in Thailand. The study utilizes a three-year dataset from the company's sales system database. The research methodology consists of three essential steps: 1. Event Log Format Presentation, 2. Data Import into Fluxicon Disco Software, and 3. Data Analysis with Process Mining. The outcomes of this investigation underscore the effectiveness of process mining in revealing key insights, including extended waiting times for quotation approvals, frequent requests for quotation modifications, and notable challenges within the system. By analyzing the workload of employees, this research provides a framework for troubleshooting sales system issues, offering a pathway for enhancing quotation approval processes and reducing the frequency of quotation corrections. In today's era of perpetual digital transformation and relentless competition, this research positions itself as a model for effective digital transformation within organizations, seeking to drive essential changes that align with the evolving landscape of the digital age.  © 2023 IEEE.
