AB  - Process mining is a young research discipline combining process and data science to analyze processes. Part of the success of process mining can arguably be attributed to the availability of open-source tools, datasets and standards that facilitate the exchange of ideas. The current leading process mining frameworks, ProM and PM4Py, present different tradeoffs in terms of scalability, ease-of-use, and feature completeness. We present ProM4Py, a Python wrapper for the ProM framework combining the scalability and feature-richness of ProM with PM4Py’s ease-of-use. ProM4Py seamlessly integrates with PM4Py, such that existing PM4Py scripts can be migrated to it with minimal code changes. © 2024 Copyright for this paper by its authors.
