AB  - This demo paper introduces CSV-PM-LLM-Parsing, a Python library to automatically transform unstructured event logs contained in CSV files into process mining event logs by using Large Language Models (LLMs). In particular, we implement modules for three problems: 1) identification of the separator and quote character, 2) selection of the essential process mining columns, and 3) timestamp format detection. Our library is compatible with any LLM supporting the OpenAI’s API specification. Our experiment shows that some LLMs (such as gpt-4o or the open-source Qwen/Qwen2-72B-Instruct) can effectively tackle all three problems. The source code is publicly available in the Git repository https://github.com/fit-alessandro-berti/csv-pm-llm-parsing. © 2024 Copyright for this paper by its authors.
