AB  - Logs have been used in modern software solutions for development and maintenance purposes as they are able to represent a rich source of information for subsequent analysis. A line of research focuses on the application of artificial intelligence techniques on logs to predict system behavior and to perform anomaly detection. Successful industrial applications are rather sparse due to the lack of publicly available log datasets. To fill this gap, we developed a method to synthetically generate a log dataset, which resembles a linear program execution log file. In this paper, the method is described as well as existing datasets are discussed. The generated dataset should enable a possibility for researcher to have a common base for new approaches. © 2022, The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG.
