AB  - With the advent of the era of big data, enterprises pay increasing attention to the business process information recorded in the business system, which plays an important role in optimizing the business process. The smooth operation of warehousing business process can save operation time and cost for enterprises to a great extent. In this paper, it is proposed a Petri net which reflects the real warehousing and out-storage process of the enterprise. Specifically, the event log stored in the enterprise business system is obtained. As for building the Petri net, Prom software and α algorithm are applied to mine the event log. Then, the real event log is replayed on the Petri net of the theoretical warehousing process for consistency checking. Finally, the problems arise in the consistency checking results are analyzed and solved, and the original Petri net are improved. © 2021, The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG.
