AB  - The main goal of this article is to improve the methods for analyzing and forecasting indicators of business processes in social systems. The task was to minimize the factor of subjective perception of business processes by analysts and reduce the complexity of building business process models. The second task of the article is to use for the prediction of parameters, not a simulation model, but analytical expressions describing the laws of probability distribution of parameter values. It was expected that this would reduce the complexity of building predictive models and analyzing the system under study. The object of the study was the process of teaching students in the discipline “Discrete Mathematics” using learning management system (LMS) Moodle.The article uses the following methods and technologies: the collection of primary data on the business processes of the research object was performed using LMS Moodle; identification of the business process model based on the information system data using the Process Mining methods and ProM 6 software; prediction of system operation parameters—total process execution time and complexity using the GERT network apparatus and agent simulation models; comparative assessment of the predictive power of approaches to the prediction of indicators of the object of study. The study showed that the applied approach really allows to increase the objectivity of the study, as well as reduce the complexity of the forecast. The assessment of predictive power shows that the proposed approach is not inferior in prediction accuracy to traditional approaches to simulation modeling. © Springer Nature Singapore Pte Ltd. 2020.
