AB  - Software organizations produce evidence of the execution of their activities, which can be processed with algorithms, supported by process mining tools, and used to discover, monitor and improve processes. Different kinds of process mining tools have been developed, which has resulted in challenges for their selection or adoption according to the algorithms or techniques that each one of them handles. MoProPEI-MP is presented as an adaptation of a process model for information exploitation projects, oriented to guide in the identification and selection of algorithms and tools of process mining. The evaluation of the adaptation of the model was endorsed by 17 primary studies obtained from a literature review, identifying the most reported process mining tools used in software processes case studies. Also, it presents the traceability with all the tasks of the activities of MoProPEI-MP. © 2018 Academia. All rights reserved.
